{# Consent toggle on the account overview.

   The handler lives in an onchange ATTRIBUTE, not in a <script> tag, and that is
   the entire point of this template. Two facts about the storefront made every
   other approach fail:

   1. Markup that the application injects with innerHTML never executes inline
      scripts. A <script> next to the form worked on the first full page load and
      was dead on every later visit.
   2. An onchange attribute is an attribute. It is compiled when the element is
      created, so it keeps working on a form that arrived through innerHTML. That
      is why this one is an attribute and not a listener attached from a script.

   data-form-auto-submit is deliberately not used. It would need
   PluginManager.initializePlugins(), and main.js calls that only on
   DOMContentLoaded and inside the plugin's own ajax callback, so nothing re-binds
   plugins after an in-app navigation. It also wants an ajaxContainerSelector,
   and _onAfterAjaxSubmit replaces that container with innerHTML, which brings
   back point 1 for every subsequent toggle.

   The handler is handed `this` and not `this.form`: HTMLFormElement.form is null
   on the form element itself, which is a silent way to pass null into the
   callback and abort before the request is ever made.

   Without JavaScript the checkbox cannot change the state by itself, so
   <noscript> carries the submit button. Scripting-enabled browsers do not render
   noscript content, including when it is inserted with innerHTML, so the button
   appears exactly when it is needed and never otherwise.
#}
{% set consentActive = topdataReviewReminderConsent.isActive(context) %}

<form name="reviewReminderConsent"
      method="post"
      action="{{ path('account.reviewReminder.consent') }}"
      onchange="(function (form) {
          var box = form.querySelector('input[type=checkbox]');
          fetch(form.action, {
              method: 'POST',
              body: new FormData(form),
              credentials: 'same-origin',
              headers: { 'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest' }
          })
              .then(function (response) {
                  if (!response.ok) { throw new Error(response.status); }
                  return response.json();
              })
              .then(function (data) {
                  // The database decides, not the request: a stale tab or a double
                  // click can never leave the box showing something else.
                  box.checked = !!data.active;
              })
              .catch(function () {
                  // No fetch, no JSON, offline — post the form natively. The route
                  // redirects back to the account overview.
                  form.submit();
              });
      })(this)">
    <div class="form-check">
        {# An unchecked box contributes nothing at all to the body, so the route
           reads a missing `option` as a withdrawal. Only option=subscribe opts in. #}
        <input type="checkbox"
               class="form-check-input"
               id="reviewReminderConsent"
               name="option"
               autocomplete="off"
               value="subscribe"
               {% if consentActive %}checked="checked"{% endif %}>

        <label class="form-check-label custom-control-label" for="reviewReminderConsent">
            {{ topdataReviewReminder.translate(context.languageInfo.localeCode, 'consentLabel') }}
        </label>
    </div>

    <p class="mb-0 mt-2 small text-muted">
        {{ topdataReviewReminder.translate(context.languageInfo.localeCode, 'consentHint') }}
    </p>

    <noscript>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm mt-2">
            {{ topdataReviewReminder.translate(context.languageInfo.localeCode, 'consentSave') }}
        </button>
    </noscript>
</form>
